KG42.register("rules-af0ca2ce4fc03e64a4f110d3",{"id":"45-heat_pump_flexibility::v141-c-R005","paper":"45-heat_pump_flexibility","record":{"rule_id":"v141-c-R005","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","name":"Local market coordinator","process_stage":"coordination","market_meaning":"Demand submissions provide bids to the local market operator, which organizes them in decreasing order to establish the demand curve. Scope: Centralized two-sided auction in the modeled local electricity market. Supply offers provide inputs to the local market operator, which organizes them in increasing order to establish the supply curve. Scope: Centralized two-sided auction in the modeled local electricity market.","independence_rationale":"Relations governed by the approved function coordination.local_operator under the fixed relation-ownership template. Conditional branches retain their explicit scope in local constraints.","V":["bidding.demand","bidding.supply","coordination.local_operator"],"E":[{"edge_id":"v141-c-R005-E001","source":"bidding.demand","target":"coordination.local_operator","type":"links","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R005-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e08","v141-b-g01-e10"]},{"edge_id":"v141-c-R005-E002","source":"bidding.supply","target":"coordination.local_operator","type":"links","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R005-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e10"]}],"omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"coordination","context_text":"Centralized two-sided auction in the modeled local electricity market.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e08","v141-b-g01-e10"]},"x":[],"theta":[],"phi":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R005-C001","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"Demand submissions provide bids to the local market operator, which organizes them in decreasing order to establish the demand curve. Scope: Centralized two-sided auction in the modeled local electricity market.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["bidding.demand","coordination.local_operator"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e08","v141-b-g01-e10"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R005-C002","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"Supply offers provide inputs to the local market operator, which organizes them in increasing order to establish the supply curve. Scope: Centralized two-sided auction in the modeled local electricity market.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["bidding.supply","coordination.local_operator"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e10"]}],"pi":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e08","location":{"location_id":"src-115be449fd-p04-c1r3__v141-a-M01-bidding","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"Limited by the scope, the description of other parts of lemlab is omitted Th in this work. However, ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"The local electricity market proposed in this study adopts a centralized two-sided auction format, similar to wholesale electricity markets. Agents submit their bids to a market operator at a time interval in a standardized bid format. The objective of the market is to maximize social welfare [18]."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e10","location":{"location_id":"src-115be449fd-p04-c1r4__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"interval in a standardized bid format. The objective of the market is 𝛥𝑝 to maximize social welfare ","equation_id":"1","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"The bids and offers are denoted as d_i and s_j, respectively. n_B and n_S represent the number of buyers and sellers. To achieve maximum social welfare, the market operator organizes the bids in decreasing order and offers in increasing order, establishing the demand and supply curve. The intersection of the demand and supply curve is known as the market closing price, which is then communicated to each agent and used for settlement."}],"field_notes":{"empty_E_reason":null,"empty_x_reason":"No design or operational variable is declared because this rule only prescribes how the local market operator orders bids and offers that have already been submitted. The supplied passage does not define a per-bid price or other sort-key variable for this rule; d_i and s_j are used in the adjacent welfare-balance equation as bid/offer quantities, so treating them as the ordering variables would be unsupported.","empty_theta_reason":"No fixed parameter is declared for this rule. The supplied evidence introduces n_B and n_S as counts in the adjacent welfare-balance passage, but does not define them as parameters of a formal ordering constraint, and the ordering key itself is missing."},"evidence_basis":"explicit","implementation_status":"unimplemented","status":"needs_review","lead_ids":["v141-a-M01-bidding","v141-a-M01-clearing","v141-a-M01-matching","v141-a-M01-pricing","v141-a-M01-settlement"],"extras":{"decision_anchor":"coordination.local_operator","graph_fact_supports":[[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e08","quote":"Agents submit their bids to a market operator at a time interval in a standardized bid format."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e10","quote":"To achieve maximum social welfare, the market operator organizes the bids in decreasing order and offers in increasing order, establishing the demand and supply curve."}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e10","quote":"To achieve maximum social welfare, the market operator organizes the bids in decreasing order and offers in increasing order, establishing the demand and supply curve."}]],"C2_formalization":{"graph_sha256":"fde42709465cf2847acac217c583a7c22e1e5fa596991ac7e2184bbfdeceb966","applicability":"needs_revision","reason":"Provisional assessment from the supplied unreviewed B evidence. The source supports the procedural direction of this coordination rule: the local market operator organizes demand bids in decreasing order and supply offers in increasing order to establish the demand and supply curves. However, the supplied passage does not define the ordering key or a per-bid/per-offer price symbol for this operation; d_i and s_j appear in the adjacent welfare-balance equation as bid/offer quantities. Treating d_i and s_j themselves as the sort keys would be an unsupported interpretation. I therefore preserve both procedural constraints as not_formalized and request B re-extraction of the missing sort-key definitions before writing a mathematical ordering constraint. This is not a claim that the rule is non-mathematical; it is an unresolved source-definition gap.","bindings":[],"revision_requests":["Request B re-extraction of the per-bid demand price (or other ordering-key) symbol and the per-offer supply price (or other ordering-key) symbol used by the local market operator when it organizes demand bids in decreasing order and supply offers in increasing order. The supplied passage defines d_i and s_j in the welfare-balance equation as bid/offer quantities but does not define the key for the stated ordering.","Request explicit source clarification whether the stated decreasing/increasing order is by price, quantity, or another standardized bid attribute in the modeled centralized two-sided auction."]}},"quarantined_references":[]}});
